# punused findings adjudicated for this repo. One literal substring per line,
# matched against punused's output line; full-line `#` comments carry the reason.
#
# punused asks gopls for `textDocument/references` and reports a declaration with
# none. A method that exists ONLY to satisfy an interface has no direct reference
# by construction: the caller holds the interface, not the concrete type. Deleting
# one does not remove dead code, it removes an interface implementation, and the
# type stops satisfying its contract.

# --- static_persist.go's in-memory overlay: every entry below is an interface
# method invoked by net/http through fs.FS, and each is required for the served
# bytes to be correct rather than optional.
#
# The overlay swaps ONE file's content inside the embedded static FS so the
# persistence flag reaches the page. http.FileServer then drives it:
#
#   fs.ReadDir  -> overlayFS.ReadDir   (directory enumeration; the overlay adds
#                                       and removes no entries, so it delegates)
#   fs.File     -> memFile.Stat/Read/Close/Seek
#                                      (Seek is not optional: http.ServeContent
#                                       needs an io.Seeker to size the body and to
#                                       answer a Range request. Without it the
#                                       overlaid file is refused.)
#   fs.FileInfo -> memInfo.Name/Size/Mode/ModTime/Sys
#                                      (ModTime is deliberately the zero time,
#                                       matching embed.FS, so no Last-Modified
#                                       appears on one file and not its
#                                       neighbours; the content-hash ETag is the
#                                       validator.)
#
# static_persist.go also carries compile-time assertions that these types satisfy
# fs.ReadDirFS, fs.File and fs.FileInfo, so dropping a method is a build failure
# rather than a 500 on one asset. The behaviour is covered end to end by
# TestPersistFlagReachesTheServedPage and
# TestPersistFlagOverlayKeepsTheServedBytesSelfConsistent.
method (overlayFS).ReadDir
method (*memFile).Stat
method (*memFile).Read
method (*memFile).Seek
method (*memFile).Close
method (memInfo).Name
method (memInfo).Size
method (memInfo).Mode
method (memInfo).ModTime
method (memInfo).Sys
